- “Derivative Work” means a modification or adaptation of the Software, or a work that incorporates all or part of the Software code, made by You or on Your behalf under the rights granted by this License. Using the Software as a development or testing harness does not by itself make a separate project or its output a Derivative Work. A separate project’s independently authored code, data, and assets are not a Derivative Work if they do not include Software code; their copyrights remain with their respective creators. This License applies to the CHOAM-owned or CHOAM-licensed portions of a Derivative Work and does not transfer ownership of Your independently authored additions. Software and Derivative Works do not include third-party components except to the extent CHOAM owns or is authorized to license rights in them.
- “Discodex Module” means any separable source-code or binary-code module taken or extracted from the Software or a Derivative Work, whether or not the module implements a convenience feature.
- “You” means the person or legal entity exercising rights under this License.
- “Affiliate” means an entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with You. “Control” means direct or indirect ownership of more than 50% of the voting interests or the power to direct management.
- “Product” means a separately marketed or separately released game, application, service, or other commercial offering that (a) distributes or makes the Software or a Derivative Work available to users, (b) makes the Software or a Derivative Work available through a hosted or managed service, or (c) includes or executes a Discodex Module as part of the offering’s operation. A call to the Software solely for development or testing is Development Harness Use, not Product operation. Independently authored code, data, or assets that do not include Software code do not by themselves make the separate project a Product. Each separately sold or separately released title or service counts as a separate Product. Revenue of You and Your Affiliates from the same Product is aggregated.
- “Development Harness Use” means calling or otherwise using the Software solely as a development or testing harness to create or test a separate project, where that project neither distributes or provides access to the Software or a Derivative Work nor includes or executes a Discodex Module in its operation. Development Harness Use is free regardless of the separate project's revenue. A separate project’s independently authored code, data, and assets that do not include Software code remain separate works with their own copyrights, even when created using the Software as a harness.
- “Net Revenue” means all revenue You or Your Affiliates receive from a Product, including sales, in-app purchases, subscriptions, advertising, and sponsorship tied to the Product, less (a) fees retained by stores, platforms, or payment processors, (b) refunds and chargebacks, and (c) value-added, sales, and similar taxes collected from buyers.
