3. Royalty and reporting

3.1 For each Product and each Quarter, no royalty is due on the first KRW 10,000,000 of Net Revenue.

3.2 You owe CHOAM a royalty of 1% only on the portion of that Product's Net Revenue for that Quarter above KRW 10,000,000. The threshold is calculated separately for each Product and resets each Quarter; no amount carries over between Products or Quarters.

3.3 Revenue received in a currency other than KRW must be converted to KRW using the Bank of Korea base exchange rate for the last business day of the applicable Quarter.

3.4 Within 45 days after the end of each Quarter in which a royalty is due, You must send CHOAM a statement identifying each Product for which a royalty is due and showing its Net Revenue and royalty due for that Quarter. You must pay the royalty with that statement to the account CHOAM provides on request. No report is required for a Quarter in which no royalty is due. No separate reporting or license-management fee is charged.

